<title>UK: Xenova shoots up on Parke-Davies drugs deal.</title>
<headline>Xenova shoots up on Parke-Davies drugs deal.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British biotech company Xenova Group Plc jumped as high as 330 pence, up 36 pence or more than 10 percent, on Thursday after the company said it had sealed a further drug discovery collaboration with the Parke-Davies arm of US based Warner Lambert Co.</p>
<p>At 0905 GMT, the shares stood at 322 1/2 pence.</p>
<p>&quot;This is good for Xenova and the reaction of the market has been very clear on this,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>Xenova said in a statement it would receive research, milestone and royalty payments for any drugs developed through the collaboration as well as exclusive marketing rights in Europe to any new cancer drugs.</p>
<p>-- Christian Gutlederer, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
